Reece:

Try using a SCSI CD-ROM. SRM thinks all drives connected to the system
are SCSI, and if it's going to the SCSI card to look for the IDE
CD-ROM, it's going to take a dump and "fail to open" it.

If you don't have access to a SCSI CD-ROM, then try pulling the SCSI
card, and installing to an IDE hard drive, and use the SCSI for /home
or /usr after you've gotten Linux installed.

I know it's not much, but I hope it helps.

-SSB

