> Actually, this is rather simple. Try the "help" command at the SRM
> console, and also "help aDVANCED", "help seT" and "help shOW". These
> will give you an explanation of the possible variable settings and
> commands for your firmware.
>
> If your command line above is correct, you have to enter the following
> commands at the SRM prompt in order to boot without user interaction:
>
> set aUTO_ACTION 2
> set bootdEF_DEV dka0
> set boot_OSFLAGS 0
>
> In place of the "2", you can specify "boot". You can abbreviate
> variable names by typing only the leftmost letters (you'll have to
> enter enough letters to distinguish the variable from others with the
> same beginning, of course, otherwise you'll get the error "?23 AMB
> SYM".) Just leave out the capital letters in my examples.
>
> With linux, you should use firmware ROM version 1.7, type "show confIG"
> at the SRM prompt to verify this.
>
> Viele Gruesse, Christoph
>




