I have never used an Alpha in my life, but i had a similar problem when 
installing Redhat on two oldish Sun Sparcstations at home. What the 
problem was is the old boot loaders cannot read past 1024 mb on the disk. 
One would think the install programs would be clever enough to install it 
in a usable order, but they dont. The way i got around the problem was to 
make a 100 mb /boot partition at the front of the first disk. This means 
that the bootloader can read it properly. 
This may have no relevance to Alpha's because it occurs because of the 
buggy Sun proms. But it is worth a try, especially if you are already used 
to reinstalling it. 

