A comment.  The above indeed does work but for dumping FAT partition
tables (to a file on a hard disk or on a floppy or to a printer)
I normally use sfdisk.  An advantage is that you can feed saved data
from stdin to sfdisk and it will recreate the original; even after
you managed to mess it up royally. :-)

I was actually using that also to rewrite partition tables (say,
partitions were not in order).  Dump, get data into an editor, do
adjustments and feed results back into sfdisk.  A brand new partition
table with a minimum of typing, intact file systems, and very little
chance of a screwup.

Unfortunately sfdisk does not work on BSD type partition tables. :-(

  Michal


