Hi Guys,

You might want to setup a ramdisk and go that route.  I was having the same
problems installing RH 6.0 (and 6.2) on a sx164 and that fixed the problem.
I think it tried to write to /tmp on your root (in this case on the CD) and
it of course failed.  Hence, panic.  Instead, if you try something like:

boot scd0:/kernels/generic.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1

you should be able to get going.  The only caveat is that when you create
the floppy with the ramdisk (using ramdisk.img and either rawrite or dd)
make very sure you get the ramdisk.img off the images directory on the CD
you're trying to install from.

Good luck,

Rick.

P.s., I just read Bob's comment about not having a floppy; can you point it
to a writeable, formatted slice on your hd?  Maybe to the milo boot
partition?  Or if you could burn your own cd and customize it?





