I installed RH6.2 on my multia simply by downloading and dd'ing the milo
(udb-noname.img), boot (generic.img),
 and root (ramdisk.img),  from  emperor.alpha-processor.com,  for example,
(or use one of the mirrors listed on http://www.redhat.com/mirrors.html)
booting the milo disk, then the boot disk, then the root disk, and that
takes you into the install.  Select FTP or HTTP install, give it the site
you want to install from, and the path to the base directory.  for
emperor.alpha-processor.com, this was /pub/redhat/redhat-6.2/alpha.

I installed a minimal installation, as the Multia is set up a the firewall
for my internal network.  Across the cable modem, install time took a
total of about 2 hours.

I can't see why debian or turbolinux wouldn't be the same method.  The
README.install should have the procedures laid out.




