Pat Gunn (qc@apk.net) wrote:

: aboot has a 'ls' command?

Here is help message from the current 'aboot' (which is a version
0.7a):

Commands:
 h, ?                   Display this message
 q                      Halt the system and return to SRM
 p 1-8                  Look in partition <num> for configuration/kernel
 l                      List preconfigured kernels
 d <dir>                List directory <dir> in current filesystem
 b <file> <args>        Boot kernel in <file> (- for raw boot)
 i <file>               Use <file> as initial ramdisk
                        with arguments <args>
 0-9                    Boot preconfiguration 0-9 (list with 'l')

So no exactly 'ls' but there is 'd', which is doing practically the
same, and 'p' which is normally all what you want. :-)

You can find rpms for aboot-0.7a (sources and binaries), plus a small
fix in isomarkboot, on ftp://ftp.harddata.com/pub/

