SRM was in all 433a's after the 2nd month of mfg. (DEC 97)  The delay was
due to some SRM qual  work that needed to be completed. The platform was
multi os, the "a" series just designated a varient that contained options
that were not supported by SRM or UNIX.  ( like the Adaptec )


During power-up self test press the F-2 key(setup)   select - cmos setup,
press F6 key (advanced cmos-setup)  2/3 down the screen is the console
selection..

Before you do this... be sure you have a qlogic scsi ctlr,  If you have an
adaptec, you will have to stay in alpha-bios.

to install using alphabios,  you have to create a milo disk and a ramdisk,
The images are on the RH cd.

Jumpstart only works with the SRM console..

