You can go above 1024 cylinders on an alpha.  My 16gb ide disk's geometry
is as follows:

Disk /dev/hda: 16 heads, 63 sectors, 32760 cylinders
Units = cylinders of 1008 * 512 bytes

   Device Boot    Start       End    Blocks   Id  System
/dev/hda1             1     16380   8255488+  83  Linux
/dev/hda2         16381     32760   8255520   83  Linux

You should be able to change the default geometry to something matching
your drive in BIOS.  I take it that this is a spare disk?

While it's certainly not required, a later version of the OS is a good
idea since kernel pre-2.2.16 has a security hole, etc.

Regards,

Tony Hammitt


