acs,

If booting Mandrake from MILO is identical to RedHat then it should be
fairly straightforward.  You need to have that small DOS partition at
the begining of your drive and then you need to dd your MILO boot
floppy to this partition (dd if=/dev/fd0 of=/dev/[YOURPARTITIONHERE]).
According to the RedHat installation notes you should do this before
rebooting during the installation process (after the package install,
but before the X configuration).

I used the ARC boot menu and added a boot selection with linload.exe as
the OSLOADER and my MILO image as the OSLOADFILENAME.  Then to get
Linux to boot automatically I added the following to OSLOADOPTIONS:

boot sda7:/vmlinuz root=/dev/sda5

That will be passed to MILO when Linux Loader runs.  And that should be
it :)  You have to substitute your hard drives, partitions and kernel
names, but that should be the general format.

Here are some URL's that may be helpful:

http://gatekeeper.dec.com/pub/Digital/Linux-
Alpha/Miniloader/docs/HOWTO/milo.howto.html

http://www.redhat.com/support/manuals/RHL-6.2-Manual/multi-arch/s1-cd-
rom-gui-installmilo.html

Hope this helps.

Regards,
Andy.



