Hallo h0l0gRaM!

 h> So ,are Alphas moving to big endian ?
 h> Or are they staying in little endian ?

As nowadays there is no obvious advantage in being big endian, and
switching to big endian (i.e. removing little endian mode) would mean
probably a lot of changes in all supported operating systems on Alpha,
I don't think they will switch to big endian any time soon. Of course,
only Compaq knows ... but I think that Alpha CPUs will continue to
support both modes, and operating systems will continue to use that
mode that they use currently (namedly, little endian for the most
common ones Tru64, OpenVMS, Linux, Free-, Open- and NetBSD). Supporting
both little AND big endian is a compatibility issue that will probably
remain forever in Alpha CPU's, just as the real mode will remain in
mainstream Intel CPU's just about forever ...

Viele Gruesse,
Tobias



