Back before NT was popular and Sun, HP and SGI owned the workstation market,
Digital used to get "beat up" by our customers and software partners for
being different than the other majors. Funny how things change. Now, we're
actually looked on favorably for being little endian, same as the Wintel
world and Sun and HP are the ones being bitten over endianism!

All Alpha's are capable of running in either big or little endian mode
(though not both at the same time). This will probably continue as the
Himalaya platform migrates from the Mips platform to Alpha; NSK is a big
endian OS. Though don't hold me to that 'cause I'm not involved in that
migration in any way.

