Centuries ago, Nostradamus foresaw a time when Carlos would say:
>Pardon for the ignorance, but:  could anyone explain why little/big endian
>is better?  An why should I be concerned with it?

Both directions have some advantages and disadvantages; the classic paper
on this was presented in Computer Language in the 1980s, and essentially
compared it to the Jonathan Swift story of the people that had a war
over which end of a boiled egg should be placed "on top."

You should probably be concerned with the issue insofar as you need to
make sure your byte ordering of data is compatible with the systems you
plan to use that data on.
