Carlos (carlos@no_spam.no_spam.no_spam) wrote:

: Pardon for the ignorance, but:  could anyone explain why little/big endian
: is better?  An why should I be concerned with it?

If you do not write your own programs, you shouldn't. Even if you write
your own programs, but avoid using binary files for data exchange, and do 
not rely on any particular layout of your data structures beyond that is 
guaranteed by the languages you are using, you still shouldn't. On the
other hand, if you do either one of these things (and, usually, you'd
be doing either none, of both, of them ;-)), you'd better know and care
about endianness ...

Cheers,

