Carlos wrote:
> Pardon for the ignorance, but:  could anyone explain why little/big endian
> is better?  An why should I be concerned with it?

There is no "better" endianness... they are just different.

Think of it like an automobile's electrical system.  Most are negative
ground, some were positive ground (but I think few are left, if any). 
They both work equally well, but you must be aware of the difference if
e.g. you jumpstart one from the other.

Jeff



