The only thing you did wrong, is you are trying to boot the image you
removed

0:2/vmlinuz-2.2.14-6.0 root=/dev/sda3
0: = aboot flag
2 = partition 2 (/boot)
/vmlinuz-2.2.14-6.0  = the kernel in partition 2 (/boot)  to boot.
root=/dev/sda3  = where / (root is)

Edit your   /etc/aboot.conf  so 0: points to your new kernel.


JJ

