Netscape shows a different behaviour regarding dns-lookups than most
other applications.
It spawns childs (dns-helper) to prevent hanging because of (blocking)
dns-lookups.
There might a part of your problem be.
Did you check (ls -lu) if netscape really reads (whether directly or
not) /etc/svc.conf ?
Did you run tcpdump to determine if there are any differences between a
netscape-startup for nis-users and non nis-users?



