Thomas:

These systems take a long time to boot up.  It can take a few minutes before
the system actually puts a video signal to the monitor.
Did the system come with ram, or did you add it yourself?  These systems
require 72 pin True Parity simms.  Won't work with anything else.
I'm assuming that you've changed the Bios battery, and also measured the
power outputs on the supply.
Which VGA cards have you tried?  Some are not supported by Alpha.
It could also be starting in the serial mode (headless).   There is a jumper
on the MB that selects this feature.  If it's booting headless, the monitor
will never come on.
Try hooking a PC to the serial line, terminal settings are 9600,N,7.

I've had mine up and running for the last 6 months with only one re-boot.
(power failure).  It's running Linux, but also boots Win NT Server.

Good luck!
Tom Crabtree

