It sounds like a PC164UX or PC164LX. The easiest way to figure it out 
would be to turn it on and see what firmware it has. Does it say "Alpha
BIOS" or "SRM" or "ARCS BIOS"??? If it's AB or SRM it is a LX, if it 
says ARCS then it is a UX. 

Another way would be to look inside it and see if it has 4 or 6 DIMM 
slots? IIRC the LX had 4 and the UX had 6. Ohh and the UX has onboard 
ethernet. 

FYI there is a mostly complete list of Alphas and their alias at 
<http://lully.debian.org/~chris/sys_types.html>. 



HTH,

Ron



