"Daniel E. Maddux" wrote:

> You might look at IntraServer at http://www.intraserver.com.  I have an
> IntraServer 61xx (53C895 Ultra2W SCSI) running just fine in my UP2000.
>
> Daniel

The PC164 srm won't recognize the 53C895 & so can't be the boot device
adapter. It will recognize an 875 on the ITI4000 series cards and many generic
brands. Only the ITI series are accepted by the Intraserver drivers embedded
in OpenVMS an TRU64. (Generic 875 cards are marked offline.) Under Linux, all
work happily..

The Qlogic ISP1040 is recognized, but there have been comments about a bug in
the early series that VMS & TRU64 won't run with (ie get an official DEC card
and it will work).

HTH.

Evan




