Human (being@world.org) wrote:

: The aboot is used by Alpha Linux only.  You have to install aboot onto
: your harddisk.  No floppy boot is available for SRM.

I do not know if this is correct for a specific case of Avanti but
in general you can boot from floppies and SRM (a floppy in SRM is
called 'dva0').  A floppy image on RH 6.2 distribution CD creates
an SRM bootable floppy and you can also make your own with a help
of 'e2writeboot' utility from 'aboot' package.  'e2writeboot' requires
ext2 file system on a floopy you are going to use.

RH 6.2 distribution CDs (if original, or written from iso images on
the net, or made bootable with 'isomarkboot') will also work as
boot media from SRM.

  Michal



