Hm?  Sounds like it.

: Question C)
: Has anyone experienced the hanging during RH6.2 install?

Happens.  This is somewhat inconvenient but minor if you have
a system already installed. :-)

: Question D)
: Does the RH6.2 CD put install aboot as the default loader?

Depends where you hanged. :-)

If bootblock not yet on your hard drive then boot from CD but give it
'root=<your root partition here>' as a root location.  Run 'swriteboot'
to write a boot block on your hard drive.  You may want to run
'abootconf' after that to make that more convenient.  Read aboot
documentation and write /etc/aboot.conf (one again, not required at all
but saves a lot on typing and associated mistakes).  Reboot to check
that everything is correct (once you did things properly you should be
able to boot from SRM with a default kernel and configuration by typing
'b -fl 0'). Set your SRM to autoboot on powerup if so desired.

  Michal



