Ok guy's

    1. stay away from arc/alphabios, support for it  (the firmware) is going
away.

    2. The SRM Unix palcode is much better than the OEM palcode that's
included in milo.

    3. the RH install will create fat partitions by default unless you add
"expert text" to the -fl string and click the fdisk checkbox on the
"installation type selection screen."

    4. FAT partitions (DISK DRUID) are NOT compatible with SRM or ABOOT  you
must use BSD (fdisk option "b" ) labels with SRM.

    5. use the jumpstart CD, it sets it all up, your hard drive is bootable
before you even install Linux.  The RH install will detect the BSD labels
and WILL NOT try to create fat partitions.

    6. the jumpstart cd work on most all DEC Alpha's. (except axp150 maybe..
they were working on it  check the readme)


http://www.linuxalpha.compaq.com/jumpstart/


JJ






