what was the boot command you used, and what type of Alpha (Model) box.
Most likely you did not specify where root was.

typically a boot flag is passed on the command line
example for redhat on a xp1000:
boot dqa0  -fi /kernels/generic.gz -fl "root=/dev/hda expert text"

or for a serial console install
boot dqa0 -fi /kernels/generic.gz -fl "root=/dev/hda console=ttyS0 expert
text"

hda: because the CD is a IDE drive on the xp1000 and most all newer Alpha's

