>"unsupported" cards to work under Alpha Linux, and if it's worth the
>time to do the download and build to get this to work, or should I just
>get one of the "Supported" cards for the box.

I think I tried a Trident card once, a few years ago; _definitely_ no
success.

The problem, you see, is that there are some graphics cards that require
fairly "intimate" use of 16 bit values.  This is Not Particularly
Efficient on a 32 bit architecture, but is downright inefficient on
the 64 bit Alpha architecture.

As a result, there are a number of such cards that, due to requiring
a lot of "work that will be inefficient," nobody bothered to do an
Alpha port for.

You could fight your way through to a port, perhaps; you'd have a
big "burn" to performance that would essentially waste the merits
of your Alpha box.  It would be pretty dumb to spend the money to
get an Alpha box, and then waste 30% of its performance on a
lousy graphics card...
