The typical way to use MILO is from ARC but I *think* (it's been a while since I've done this) that
you can boot off a MILO floppy from SRM.  If that's the case, you can just set up the proper
environmental variables in SRM to boot the floppy with the proper flags (ie. the name of the kernel,
root partition).

However, your best bet is to find one of the cheap, but supported, video cards.  You can probably
find a used S3 or S3 ViRGE somewhere, for a really good price, rather than dropping $100 for a
Voodoo.  (Although, the Permedia2 I bought wasn't very expensive and performed like a champ).

